# 4. Technical Findings

## 4.1 Detection Overview

Endpoint telemetry was collected via Sysmon and forwarded to the Wazuh Manager for correlation.

A custom detection rule (**Rule ID 100002**) was authored to identify execution of **Mimikatz** by inspecting the `win.eventdata.originalFileName` field within Sysmon Event ID 1 (Process Creation) logs.

This field reflects the internal file metadata of the executed binary rather than its on-disk filename, allowing the rule to detect the tool even if renamed prior to execution.

---

## 4.2 MITRE ATT&CK Mapping

| ATT&CK Element | Value |
|---------------|-------|
| Tactic | Credential Access |
| Technique | T1003 – OS Credential Dumping |
| Representative Sub-technique | T1003.001 – LSASS Memory |

Mimikatz is commonly used to extract plaintext passwords, password hashes, and Kerberos tickets from LSASS process memory on Windows systems.

Adversaries typically leverage this technique to enable lateral movement and privilege escalation within a compromised environment.

