# 8. Recommendations

1. Enable Credential Guard and LSA Protection (RunAsPPL) on Windows endpoints to restrict unauthorized access to LSASS memory.
2. Deploy application allow-listing to restrict execution of unauthorized credential-access tools.
3. Ensure endpoint detection and response (EDR) and antivirus signatures remain current to detect known credential-dumping utilities and their variants.
4. Expand detection coverage beyond filename-based matching (e.g., incorporate hash-based and behavioral detections) to reduce the risk of evasion through renaming or repacking.
5. Conduct periodic purple-team exercises to validate detection and response coverage against credential-access techniques.

